An earlier clip's error does not fail the switch that took its video over.

A switch whose clip goes into the video an earlier switch is still loading
(the earlier clip not yet decoded) listened for that video's error from the
start. onReady already skips the earlier clip's first frame (patch 0027), but
the error handler did not: when the earlier clip did not decode, the newer
switch was answered failed/decode-error and dropped, and its own clip was
thrown away when it arrived. The handler now ignores an error while the video
still holds a clip this switch did not put there.

